WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.350
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.582
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.882 --> 00:00:15.135
Unit fifteen: Future Plans. In this unit, you will talk about your plans with going to.

4
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:16.907
Plan.

5
00:00:17.607 --> 00:00:20.013
Plan means something you have decided to do.

6
00:00:20.313 --> 00:00:22.034
What are your plans for the holiday?

7
00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:25.363
Your turn. Say: Plan.

8
00:00:28.063 --> 00:00:28.797
Plan.

9
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:30.750
Going to.

10
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.890
Going to means used to talk about future plans.

11
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.784
I'm going to learn to swim.

12
00:00:36.484 --> 00:00:39.322
Your turn. Say: Going to.

13
00:00:42.022 --> 00:00:43.034
Going to.

14
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:44.981
Next week.

15
00:00:45.681 --> 00:00:47.878
Next week means the week after this one.

16
00:00:48.178 --> 00:00:50.027
We're going to have a test next week.

17
00:00:50.727 --> 00:00:52.868
Your turn. Say: Next week.

18
00:00:55.568 --> 00:00:56.686
Next week.

19
00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:58.417
Visit.

20
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:01.709
Visit means to go and see a person or place.

21
00:01:02.009 --> 00:01:03.892
I'm going to visit my grandparents.

22
00:01:04.592 --> 00:01:06.769
Your turn. Say: Visit.

23
00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:10.354
Visit.

24
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.049
Learn.

25
00:01:12.749 --> 00:01:15.144
Learn means to get new knowledge or skills.

26
00:01:15.444 --> 00:01:17.060
She's going to learn the piano.

27
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.018
Your turn. Say: Learn.

28
00:01:22.718 --> 00:01:23.405
Learn.

29
00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.453
Save.

30
00:01:26.153 --> 00:01:28.350
Save means to keep money to use later.

31
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.452
I'm going to save money for a bike.

32
00:01:31.152 --> 00:01:34.083
Your turn. Say: Save.

33
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:37.505
Save.

34
00:01:38.517 --> 00:01:39.355
Future.

35
00:01:40.055 --> 00:01:41.997
Future means the time after now.

36
00:01:42.297 --> 00:01:44.459
In the future, I want to travel.

37
00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:47.196
Your turn. Say: Future.

38
00:01:49.896 --> 00:01:50.746
Future.

39
00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:52.705
Holiday.

40
00:01:53.405 --> 00:01:56.298
Holiday means a time with no school or work.

41
00:01:56.598 --> 00:01:58.609
The holiday starts next Friday.

42
00:01:59.309 --> 00:02:01.486
Your turn. Say: Holiday.

43
00:02:04.186 --> 00:02:05.036
Holiday.

44
00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.131
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:08.431 --> 00:02:10.860
Sreypich, what are you going to do next week?

46
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.951
I'm going to visit my grandparents in Kep.

47
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.217
Lovely! And in the holiday?

48
00:02:19.517 --> 00:02:21.145
I'm going to learn to swim.

49
00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.148
Any plans for the future?

50
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.508
I'm going to save money for a new bike!

51
00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:31.582
Grammar focus: Going to plus verb.

52
00:02:31.882 --> 00:02:33.789
I'm going to visit my grandparents.

53
00:02:34.089 --> 00:02:36.692
Use 'going to' for plans you decided before now.

54
00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:40.336
Now read and listen. My Plans.

55
00:02:40.636 --> 00:02:43.448
Next week, I'm going to visit my grandparents in Kep.

56
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.109
We're going to eat crab and swim in the sea.

57
00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:51.751
In the holiday, I'm going to learn to swim properly.

58
00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:55.444
I'm also going to save money for a new bike.

59
00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.887
In the future, I'm going to study hard and become a doctor.

60
00:03:01.183 --> 00:03:03.836
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:04.136 --> 00:03:05.555
I'm blank to visit my aunt.

62
00:03:05.855 --> 00:03:08.823
A, going. B, go. C, goes.

63
00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:14.747
The answer is A: going.

64
00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.203
She blank going to learn the piano.

65
00:03:18.503 --> 00:03:21.286
A, is. B, are. C, am.

66
00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:26.760
The answer is A: is.

67
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.029
The time after now is the blank.

68
00:03:30.329 --> 00:03:33.785
A, future. B, past. C, holiday.

69
00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.400
The answer is A: future.

70
00:03:40.883 --> 00:03:44.093
Now it's your turn to speak. What are you going to do next weekend?

71
00:03:49.393 --> 00:03:53.831
Next weekend, I'm going to clean my room, and then I'm going to play football with my friends.

72
00:03:54.131 --> 00:03:55.735
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.633
Great work today! You learned eight new words and going to plus verb.

74
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:05.594
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

75
00:04:05.894 --> 00:04:08.581
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.522
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

